{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The Mishkan, etc.</b> Behold the gradations of the Mishkan: they are the lower curtains. Since they spread over the Holy [Sanctuary], they are in a gradation superior to the tent and its covering, which are made of skins and do not see the face of the Holy [Sanctuary]. Therefore it does not say ״וְאֶת אָהֳלוֹ״ to equate it with it. But everything upon the lower curtains — Scripture equates them in a single gradation. And it says <b>וְאֶת מִכְסֵהוּ</b> to place it in one category together with its tent. And even if the gradation of the tent were somewhat greater than that of the covering, Scripture informs us that there is no such great difference and they are considered in a single gradation. And it says <b>אֶת קְרָסָיו</b> and does not say ״וְאֶת״, to say that this gradation of the clasps is not in the category of equivalence with the tent and its covering. And it says <b>וְאֶת קְרָשָׁיו</b> because they are equal in category with the clasps. And it says <b>אֶת בְּרִיחָיו</b> because they are not in the category of the holiness of the planks. And it says <b>אֶת עַמּוּדָיו</b> — that they are not in the category of the bars. And it says <b>וְאֶת אֲדָנָיו</b> because the pillars are equal in gradation to the sockets. And the one who understands the matter will see that the intellect recognizes the gradations as I have written."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:48.664361878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}